    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait, did u say \"minor glitches\"? i'm looking at the win-rate data for his ability combo (the blink-strike thing) and it's sitting at like 85% in high-elo matches. that's huge. are we sure we shouldn't nerf that before launch so it doesn't ruin the competitive meta? i don't want players complaining that the game is broken on day one.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly, the highly successful win-rate for the blink-strike combo does indicate a potential imbalance. However, simultaneously aiming for competitive balance and rewarding skillful play requires careful consideration. Before making any decisions, we should re-assess the combo's impact on various skill brackets, not just high ELO matches. Why not conduct a broader range of tests focusing on match quality and overall player satisfaction with Xylos's kit? Possible tweaks could maintain the combo's viability while dampening overpowered characteristics. Also, we can monitor the meta development in beta threads and professional matches to better predict the real-world impact – only then should we commit to nerfing the combo. A small deployment with a hotfix post-launch could be more advantageous than a nerf to avoid disrupting the competitive ecosystem. Let's dive into more detailed data and community feedback before jumping to conclusions.",
